#
# One ComputeClass per TPU shape. A pod asks for a shape by name and GKE builds
# a node pool for it, drawing on the reservation, then removes it once the work
# is done.
#
# This is deliberately not a node pool per shape in Terraform. That was a fixed
# partition of one reservation - so many single-chip nodes, so many eight-chip
# nodes, decided at apply time - and a run needing more of one shape queued
# behind its own ceiling while the other shape's chips sat idle. Nothing is set
# aside per shape here. The reservation is the only ceiling and Kueue decides
# who gets it.
